.TH PRTIP 1 "January 2025" "ProRT-IP 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
prtip \- modern high-performance network scanner
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B prtip
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fITARGET\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ProRT-IP WarScan
is a modern network scanner written in Rust that combines the speed of Masscan
(10M+ packets/second) with the depth of Nmap's service detection and OS
fingerprinting capabilities.
.PP
ProRT-IP supports 8 scan types (TCP SYN, Connect, UDP, FIN, NULL, Xmas, ACK,
Idle), service version detection (85-90% accuracy with 187 Nmap probes), OS
fingerprinting (16-probe technique with 2,600+ signatures), and various evasion
techniques.
.SH TARGET SPECIFICATION
Targets can be specified as:
.TP
.B Single IP
192.168.1.1
.TP
.B CIDR notation
192.168.1.0/24
.TP
.B IP range
192.168.1.1-100
.TP
.B Hostname
example.com
.TP
.B IPv6 address
2001:db8::1
.TP
.B Target file
Use \fB-iL\fR \fIfilename\fR to read targets from file
.SH PORT SPECIFICATION
.TP
.BI \-p " ports"
Specify port ranges. Examples: 80, 1-1000, 22,80,443, - (all ports)
.TP
.B \-F
Fast scan (top 100 most common ports)
.TP
.BI \-\-top\-ports " N"
Scan the N most common ports
.SH SCAN TECHNIQUES
.TP
.B \-sS
TCP SYN scan (half-open, default if privileged). Fast and stealthy.
.TP
.B \-sT
TCP Connect scan (full handshake, default if unprivileged). No privileges required.
.TP
.B \-sU
UDP scan. Discovers UDP services using protocol-specific payloads.
.TP
.B \-sF
FIN scan. Stealth scan with only FIN flag set.
.TP
.B \-sN
NULL scan. Stealth scan with no flags set.
.TP
.B \-sX
Xmas scan. Stealth scan with FIN, PSH, URG flags (lights up like a Christmas tree).
.TP
.B \-sA
ACK scan. Used to map firewall rules, not determine open/closed ports.
.TP
.BI \-sI " zombie"
Idle scan using specified zombie host. Ultimate stealth - your IP never contacts target.
.SH DETECTION OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-sV
Enable service/version detection on open ports.
.TP
.B \-O
Enable OS fingerprinting using 16-probe technique.
.TP
.B \-A
Aggressive mode. Equivalent to \fB-O -sV --progress\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-version\-intensity " 0-9"
Set service detection intensity (default: 7). Higher values are more thorough but slower.
.TP
.B \-\-banner\-grab
Enable banner grabbing for additional service information.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tls
Disable TLS/SSL service detection.
.SH TIMING AND PERFORMANCE
.TP
.BI \-T 0-5
Set timing template:
.RS
.IP T0 8
Paranoid (very slow, IDS evasion)
.IP T1 8
Sneaky (slow)
.IP T2 8
Polite (reduces load on target)
.IP T3 8
Normal (default)
.IP T4 8
Aggressive (faster)
.IP T5 8
Insane (fastest, may overwhelm targets)
.RE
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-rate " N"
Maximum packets per second.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " ms"
Connection timeout in milliseconds (default: 1000).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-retries " N"
Maximum probe retransmissions.
.TP
.BI \-\-host\-timeout " time"
Give up on host after this time (e.g., 30m, 1h).
.TP
.B \-\-adaptive\-rate
Enable adaptive rate limiting with ICMP error monitoring.
.TP
.B \-\-numa
Enable NUMA optimization for multi-socket systems (Linux only).
.SH FIREWALL/IDS EVASION
.TP
.B \-f
Fragment packets into 8-byte fragments.
.TP
.BI \-\-mtu " size"
Set custom MTU for fragmentation (must be multiple of 8).
.TP
.BI \-\-ttl " value"
Set IP Time-To-Live (1-255).
.TP
.BI \-D " decoy1,decoy2,..."
Cloak scan with decoys. Use \fBRND:N\fR for N random decoys, or \fBME\fR for your position.
.TP
.B \-\-badsum
Send packets with intentionally bad checksums (for testing).
.TP
.BI \-g " port"
Use specific source port for firewall evasion.
.SH OUTPUT OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " format"
Output format: text, json, xml (default: text)
.TP
.BI \-oN " file"
Normal text output to file.
.TP
.BI \-oX " file"
XML output to file (Nmap compatible).
.TP
.BI \-oG " file"
Greppable output to file.
.TP
.BI \-oA " basename"
Output in all formats (creates .txt, .xml, .gnmap files).
.TP
.B \-\-open
Only show open (or possibly open) ports.
.TP
.B \-v, \-vv, \-vvv
Increase verbosity level.
.TP
.B \-q
Quiet mode (suppress banner and non-essential output).
.TP
.B \-\-reason
Show reason for port state (syn-ack, rst, timeout, etc.).
.TP
.BI \-\-packet\-capture " file"
Save packets to PCAPNG file (Wireshark compatible).
.TP
.B \-\-with\-db
Enable SQLite database storage.
.SH IPv6 OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-6
Enable IPv6 only mode.
.TP
.B \-4
Enable IPv4 only mode.
.TP
.B \-\-dual\-stack
Allow both IPv4 and IPv6 targets.
.SH TUI OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-tui
Launch interactive terminal user interface with real-time dashboard.
.SH MISCELLANEOUS
.TP
.B \-\-iflist
List network interfaces and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-interface " iface"
Use specific network interface.
.TP
.B \-n
Never do DNS resolution.
.TP
.B \-Pn
Skip host discovery, treat all targets as online.
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-cdn
Skip CDN/cloud provider IP addresses.
.TP
.B \-y
Skip all confirmations (assume yes).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display help information and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B Basic SYN scan:
prtip -sS -p 1-1000 192.168.1.0/24
.TP
.B Fast scan (top 100 ports):
prtip -F 192.168.1.1
.TP
.B Service detection:
prtip -sV -p 22,80,443 target.com
.TP
.B OS fingerprinting:
prtip -O -p 1-1000 target.com
.TP
.B Aggressive scan with XML output:
prtip -A -oX scan.xml 192.168.1.0/24
.TP
.B Stealth scan with decoys:
prtip -sF -D RND:10 -p 80,443 target.com
.TP
.B Idle scan (anonymous):
prtip -sI 192.168.1.100 -p 80,443 target.com
.TP
.B IPv6 scan:
prtip -6 -p 80,443 2001:db8::1
.TP
.B TUI dashboard:
prtip --tui -sS -p 1-1000 192.168.1.0/24
.SH PRIVILEGES
Raw packet scanning (\fB-sS\fR, \fB-sU\fR, \fB-sF\fR, etc.) requires elevated privileges.
.PP
On Linux, grant capabilities instead of running as root:
.PP
.RS
sudo setcap cap_net_raw,cap_net_admin=eip /usr/local/bin/prtip
.RE
.PP
On Windows, run as Administrator.
.PP
On macOS, use sudo or configure ChmodBPF.
.PP
TCP Connect scan (\fB-sT\fR) does not require special privileges.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
General error
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments
.TP
.B 3
Permission denied
.TP
.B 4
Network error
.TP
.B 5
Target unreachable
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.prtip/config.toml
User configuration file
.TP
.I ~/.prtip/history.json
Command history (with \fB--save-history\fR)
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PRTIP_CONFIG
Path to configuration file
.TP
.B PRTIP_LOG_LEVEL
Logging level (trace, debug, info, warn, error)
.TP
.B PRTIP_NO_COLOR
Disable colored output
.SH LEGAL NOTICE
ProRT-IP is a security research tool intended for penetration testing, network
security auditing, educational purposes, and red team operations.
.PP
.B ALWAYS obtain proper authorization before scanning networks you do not own.
.PP
Unauthorized scanning may be illegal in your jurisdiction.
